#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d3b2e6-53ce-5675-9719-1e6f7e01b5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421538} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c0b97a-bdab-58f5-a07c-79787eb3f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421539} {:answer/id #uuid "bec50d68-081a-5899-b3a9-04ecbfa8e6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421540} {:answer/id #uuid "c9eefa24-dc26-5b64-9a24-78a5e468b6d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421541} {:answer/id #uuid "dd800906-eb9a-5ad2-843c-4ad00d0bcb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421543}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421538} :answer-field/id #uuid "af669ad0-ae47-5a9d-ab8c-914967692ad4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ec9f8b4-aba4-50ea-8a5e-5c6fd75fd0f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78341" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${A}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${A}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $A$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${A}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =O\\cdot O \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b883705-4f13-564f-a1ef-126507d3f930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236693} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2c609e-ade1-504f-b56a-cbe1ca68518e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236899} {:answer/id #uuid "c3feefde-7b37-5a86-8f6e-b0c208a50961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237055} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6c207b-ce5d-57b0-82bc-7b3988df6723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237330} {:answer/id #uuid "f669d9e4-9bbe-5b98-a671-93ce001f7f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237372}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237372} :answer-field/id #uuid "16abb40e-e765-53e3-90ea-7a181a9af49c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9047fc55-30cd-5bc7-96fe-e8f5b01aa182" :question/math-academy-id "q-10004" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0737fd5b-96ea-5473-a44f-a41afd6c1553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=13,\\,y=25,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235846} {:answer/id #uuid "4537e0a4-37b3-5f1d-9fed-26057698bace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236260} {:answer/id #uuid "a124349e-3884-56ce-9385-08f24fa6a176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=13,\\,y=19,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236824} {:answer/id #uuid "aad0b275-3680-5a33-969f-268cb505c79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-11,\\,y=19,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236897} {:answer/id #uuid "cf542f7a-ea1a-583f-908a-f1953ea01648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-13,\\,y=19,\\,z=57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236260} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4836e15-142a-5dba-b682-0f201894c5b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "062c7a4a-d791-5879-9bf4-0c469a15394c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10038" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z+2y+7x &=1 \\\\ 3y-z &=-2 \\\\ 4y-2z-3x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+2y+z &=1 \\\\ 3y-z &=-2 \\\\ -3x+4y-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =7\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =7(-6+4)-2(-3)+1(9) \\\\  & =-14+6+9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 9 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 34 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -34 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 77\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f4398f-18db-5bb4-ab9f-e4e728621f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235973} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7a6fdc-7ce6-5e15-89a2-84e59db68519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=15,y=10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236221} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1cb93d-039d-5852-a40e-003b41fbe609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236697} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c46c33-108b-5ebb-8533-fcb6694cba67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237004} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1a6c04-3807-5923-9a4c-3658958aaca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235973} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2b74e1-36cd-50e9-b37c-03195ff066d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a8a38c1-8d83-5c15-8052-a8f7706f20a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10074" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z &=-1-x \\\\ 4y &=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z &=0 \\\\ x+6z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $$\n\\displaystyle x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18cf84eb-8019-5024-a9d4-f6d05cfd3269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=15,y=19,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235970} {:answer/id #uuid "4f20d1b9-9c63-50d2-a24e-b400decf2a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236328} {:answer/id #uuid "5b847704-0397-5367-962e-626db03c9d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=3,y=\\frac{19}{5},z=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236389} {:answer/id #uuid "b802e7d8-4eb2-58b7-9ef0-5acd50e6d76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236989} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d25859-b8ae-5dba-8a88-d56b4edbf4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=15,y=-19,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236989} :answer-field/id #uuid "46b1f130-63be-5d63-8f37-389b677d9647" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e779cc8b-bc48-5f02-aa7a-6ab946e667e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-10075" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3z-y+x-5 &=0 \\\\ y+2x+2z &=1 \\\\ z-2x-2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=5 \\\\ 2x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ -2x-2y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1+4)+1(2+4)+3(-4+2) \\\\  & =5+6-6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -\\frac{19}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338ad7db-610c-5504-8b07-93ddf6989bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236141} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb5824f-641f-50ba-a60c-6f273e5bc745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236307} {:answer/id #uuid "87dae3e4-1d42-58e8-97db-0124534b5c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236665} {:answer/id #uuid "f5dd7272-ba74-59ef-a368-6470a994b20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237366} {:answer/id #uuid "f757ba64-10e8-5058-8e1b-0c55eb97642d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=19,y=49,z=58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236141} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd21ae35-d429-561d-927c-fa4d44ff854e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e8e08af1-fca9-5664-99a6-119c31e3f669" :question/math-academy-id "q-10076" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z &=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z &=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4128ba71-30f4-5d9f-a1da-f0feb798ee82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236233} {:answer/id #uuid "4a578053-2e19-50df-9af8-8b315860043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236294} {:answer/id #uuid "5c4620a0-76d3-5e9f-92c3-382dca21ee9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=29,y=12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236392} {:answer/id #uuid "88066dff-8cdf-5893-a4d3-81d269f7ee2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-25,y=-12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236666} {:answer/id #uuid "b8391916-39bd-5633-8b71-eb03b0decc7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-15,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236233} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7b3d13-f904-586b-ba35-a7c8c21f7369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c7f748e9-7cb4-573b-a324-159e0e3861ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-10100" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z &=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z &=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(7-2)-3(-2)+1(4-21) \\\\  & =10+6-17 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -17 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -17 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-29 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 100\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-29,y=-12,z=100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee7e0cc-1841-50f3-a5f2-a54b57df7f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=8,y=-8,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236414} {:answer/id #uuid "79759bba-4475-51ba-874e-be7acc9f35b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236581} {:answer/id #uuid "e806513b-a961-5fd9-b571-b43cd8457290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237278} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd5388f-1f93-52d6-b413-aa7b0e4d018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=8,y=8,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237302} {:answer/id #uuid "fd42bafb-20e3-522c-919b-8c6a78d5d018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236581} :answer-field/id #uuid "3334def8-af8d-5c3c-8b52-9e05eccf839f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a8cc406f-67fe-55bc-b55e-b6858ce9be1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10101" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1-3(-2))+0-1(-2-3) \\\\  & =1+6+2+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432a51a6-a859-539f-aad3-0c3afb4b46f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236251} {:answer/id #uuid "95ab3dfc-0bd9-5c63-b32d-b78ab929c832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=-4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236768} {:answer/id #uuid "c356000e-035d-577e-85f1-5fd545858205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237051} {:answer/id #uuid "c3eca95b-b2df-58cc-bfa3-67df1d256020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237054} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9f0f71-f5a0-5bca-9a3b-a6ddd72eabaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237051} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7f236a0-c448-555c-b80c-c66d10276c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "267865d4-e8c6-50f1-8813-4866781fbd07" :question/math-academy-id "q-10102" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+2z &=1 \\\\ x+y+z &=3 \\\\ y+2z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2(2)+2(1) \\\\  & =-4+2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512f4d7d-a50e-5ac1-9b00-a23a2f1e85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461195} {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3434df-a