BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{2}$; $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0172af46-e351-502b-aa3a-c62166a7ed72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ -15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235806} {:answer/id #uuid "12333d71-f54d-5f6e-9e6c-5fc764d2bc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 9 \\\\ -15 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235924} {:answer/id #uuid "442b8d6f-cd03-5b5a-84f1-23d1ca97ea2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b37a294-1d3c-567d-bf66-b3920a5fe9a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236585} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce9cddf-2413-5e15-89c7-45b259cab3b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44f4bb4-30a2-5a30-959a-18587874cdc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53274149-3160-5be4-b6eb-415d49f449f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-1033" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthen $EF=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $E$ and $4$ rows in $F,$ so $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={EF}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $EF,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,18=1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,15=3\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=3\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle EF=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7a62ec-13b8-543d-9616-121868053523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236016} {:answer/id #uuid "22e57d49-7fd7-563f-abb5-64190ff4aa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236039} {:answer/id #uuid "24e7f5a9-a414-5f74-91fa-736878205105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236055} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9d6d90-f170-5014-9e02-b7a17b19bb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236497} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d5586-3d96-5a03-86a4-ba2ed71c39b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034} :answer-field/id #uuid "c96651e8-d8ed-5375-92a8-7fde59b35ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "83b01661-23af-5f73-bcb3-22f2f416f38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1035" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $T,$ so $S$ and $T$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={ST}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $ST,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,24=2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle ST=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a4fbe6-9d29-5b7b-b18d-8f3bce272a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -30 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236166} {:answer/id #uuid "43ad9035-d025-5bfb-ac83-4d96682052ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236253} {:answer/id #uuid "67b500c4-3c08-5c55-a91d-f14b3fb90af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236472} {:answer/id #uuid "7315c044-2f4b-51a4-b2ff-d8bff4fa99f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236546} {:answer/id #uuid "9569ea85-ee3c-57f6-8cc7-7c783b778fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -50 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236546} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb8b408d-c2ca-511c-b127-d031e6c0f14e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dc228162-bbed-5edc-ac18-77311da73b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-1038" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10\\cdot 1 & -10\\cdot (-5) & -10\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 6\\cdot 1 & 6\\cdot (-5) & 6\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 8\\cdot 1 & 8\\cdot (-5) & 8\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290df338-cbf5-5bde-98fe-bac5fcf6883e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238418} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddc03a9-31e0-5513-b8a2-708a0189a34d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239146} {:answer/id #uuid "8c16ab80-c07b-5b4b-ad79-83a262db83fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239272} {:answer/id #uuid "b62a8c7a-d543-5087-9732-2e1cdd0bd83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239645} {:answer/id #uuid "e537f447-3bfe-5af5-84c5-e2af277694e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240067}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240067} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbcab08-178c-57a6-a96a-3ec75b0b9a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b86d16b9-91e7-5d11-97b1-e0f931afe9d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-104536" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-2z &=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z &=2x-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z &=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1604f16b-b6ec-5977-8db2-4745c554c4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=3,y=-11,z=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238242} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd6c920-44cd-558c-b5b5-5a4fb709b7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-11,y=6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238330} {:answer/id #uuid "37255593-62a2-5d88-b4ca-46ad8477c825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=11,y=6,z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238534} {:answer/id #uuid "862e6d9d-6938-55b2-9966-6d4c843929b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239222} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e74476-4ff0-5e8b-8dc3-25b96e048393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=6,y=-3,z=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239222} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d168cf8-68f1-5703-91a1-1c3db1aa2a7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "30372d4a-7cb0-560b-a8cf-a404cabf96f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104541" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x &=2 \\\\ -3z+y &=3 \\\\ 2x+y &=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=2 \\\\ y-3z &=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef491d6-2ab5-50e3-af24-150a984cf7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=1,y=2,z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238315} {:answer/id #uuid "6433840e-f62b-5d25-8771-780117ffbb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=1,y=1,z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238933} {:answer/id #uuid "7d19c17c-f45c-59ab-ad2c-fc3a4aac1a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=1,y=-2,z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239137} {:answer/id #uuid "e38fd3ea-ff34-57f1-b478-4bbf6667b49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=-1,y=-1,z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240056} {:answer/id #uuid "e8758369-817b-5292-aa34-f56b3a84956f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=2,y=1,z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240101}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3164e39-ba71-5ae7-8548-2f22c8c3ac60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5c5fa419-7d88-586a-9224-2f097b998fb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104546" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z+x &=2 \\\\ 2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 2z-y &=-3x+3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=2 \\\\ 2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 3x-y+2z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4-3)-0+(0-6) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373c885e-aef8-50b9-911a-ec047f2d5681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448042} {:answer/id #uuid "20c8ff2a-dc3c-5659-91b9-08202181b0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448043}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448042} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed3fa0be-e63d-5195-b281-fe8450f3750c" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015547b8-bd38-530c-8e48-88bc8e2e2e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448044} {:answer/id #uuid "1e7fb983-a1ee-5142-94cd-263cd7c41eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448045}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448045} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5993f1a-def4-558a-814a-d16d4117184e" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c83f9f-5824-5aed-81dd-43478e72282d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448046} {:answer/id #uuid "95a699cb-8161-554e-9a4d-c4e507a37e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448046} :answer-field/id #uuid "d65054a8-c89c-52ab-a032-831b9f5b6b89" :answer-field/key "$B={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9db68f61-a1ba-5fec-8a45-32913742b631" :question/math-academy-id "q-11634" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{3}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ is true. \nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "571118f7-834d-565e-8ce1-6917716176bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448048} {:answer/id #uuid "feda0f47-91fe-5b24-a64c-d9d72c65d7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448049} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f2afe7a-b39e-52d9-b782-4c29afe645ed" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4daa118-2951-524a-a8a5-a07a11973d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448050} {:answer/id #uuid "02b9525c-5aa7-5637-9eb7-f2af65078057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448051}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448050} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a46244-d72a-5634-be81-4125503e6ad9" :answer-field/key "$AD=DA={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f8c239a-1d74-5503-87f3-5a2380f75c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448052} {:answer/id #uuid "c8086890-3a86-5a1b-876b-fba7bced727e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448052} :answer-field/id #uuid "55292d74-822b-5992-b5bf-236b8ac95ebf" :answer-field/key "$D={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a987f21-4e16-5f44-b8f8-8e69cf93fc24" :question/math-academy-id "q-11636" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AD=DA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AD=DA={I}_{3}$ is false. As a result, $D\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $D={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4efcf39-ef5c-51be-9197-fd336dcc21cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448054} {:answer/id #uuid "46eb2630-2587-530d-ae7f-6568bb2b9247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448055}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448055} :answer-field/id #uuid "66536e33-097f-5b8e-aabe-387b94e6dcdf" :answer-field/key "$CD=DC={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd936360-4ab5-54cc-85f8-f730e2f97b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448056} {:answer/id #uuid "59684c94-4157-5480-bbf9-8f31eab89e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448056} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa70be3f-3e90-53c6-b327-0f504c4a38ba" :answer-field/key "$DE=ED={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c207fb4-dbd6-51a8-b240-b57b53b19e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448058} {:answer/id #uuid "0e460479-68f8-53e2-8de7-0af880f9bb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448059}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448059} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0967798-fafd-515e-b212-b3143643fbf1" :answer-field/key "$D={C}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "297364cd-4444-5a41-ba36-21b226267ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11637" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $CD=DC={I}_{2}$ is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement $D={C}^{-1}$ is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $DE=ED={I}_{2}$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $CD=DC={I}_{2}$; $D={C}^{-1}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1682dd1e-6a3e-585a-b8de-5b23b7ea94c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260072} {:answer/id #uuid "1689a068-b51c-5ee0-8061-d29ddb153fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260073} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2470ac-dd54-5b59-9478-94b73932f435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260124} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4bbf76-c7a5-5145-83ec-650fb6db1e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260964} {:answer/id #uuid "de38351b-baf5-5a90-a6e5-ee73c0a46168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261839}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261839} :answer-field/id #uuid "b65a4ca0-f974-538c-8c68-2ae22626c269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94e0f9cc-6b5b-54e5-ac6a-648684ded023" :question/math-academy-id "q-128309" :question/problem "Find the value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2(4-0)-1(1-0)-1(-3-20) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-23) \\\\  & =-8-1-23 \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "938435d8-69e4-5177-83be-c2661b220df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} {:answer/id #uuid "b0acf52f-1926-563b-90fe-5bd5c838a2cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437788} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef069a99-e51d-5c41-b3dd-fbe618b3ae29" :answer-field/key "$det(Q)=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda1810e-40d9-5b5a-8ed9-7de0e91b6696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8badb5-ccf3-54b7-bf14-15f19c3c783e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437790} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6baa2c-bfa2-5841-829c-446168fc4d31" :answer-field/key "$det(Q)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} {:answer/id #uuid "13768b60-6037-5979-87a7-85e46aa637f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437793}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} :answer-field/id #uuid "10609156-1bc3-5176-82f7-7da72d8cac5c" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45f9eaa1-ec03-587f-9925-ac1e03ddc805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667930} {:answer/id #uuid "ceeca510-070e-5b7e-a5b0-fde585d5adcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186667931} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceb5d4cf-1c76-560f-9b77-bb0950007541" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f86fe2f1-042a-5183-8a18-518a658cc1a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(9-5)-1(6-3)-1(10-9) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, none of the statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} {:answer/id #uuid "b3238a25-1600-54c9-a92e-d6b1f31166ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437795}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} :answer-field/id #uuid "0457a549-1799-5124-a11e-6cbe8bf02f40" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86770289-d595-5a74-8241-7f7eaf943501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437796} {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c446f0-c232-5d1a-a9fa-08c4d973bbe4" :answer-field/key "$T$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d221ff-7342-5189-8083-2e45e2305d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437798} {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5f6d45-4846-5d6c-b409-f20f073263eb" :answer-field/key "$det(T)=-30$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "898815e0-65a8-55f9-b81f-a64efbb5e7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-5\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$T$ is **not** a singular matrix” and $det(T)=-30$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a78a3a-a96f-5296-bb6f-17bd0c2c1029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437812} {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d87a851-8d26-5425-83e8-dba94be07b21" :answer-field/key "$R$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d06dd62-d83d-54e9-b4ea-1974429d75ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437814} {:answer/id #uuid "423c9da1-fb5c-5eb1-aac0-e8f7d5033fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437815} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad0097cd-c1c7-5438-b4af-b5844d0cf50a" :answer-field/key "$det(R)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438936} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e2b6e65-193a-5e1a-ae4e-babcf8cd0b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} {:answer/id #uuid "4daf1704-b4bb-5190-aede-54368b9e49c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437817}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437816} :answer-field/id #uuid "727b8a81-c497-5e39-8d74-82d5d2b34ab9" :answer-field/key "$det(R)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d0d8a3d8-8c1e-55f4-b495-022734d0f802" :question/math-academy-id "q-128484" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{vmatrix}-\\sqrt{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(0+\\sqrt{2})-\\sqrt{2}(2+1)+2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$R$ is a singular matrix” and $det(R)=0$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fb98df-401c-5fa9-9f2f-08261df60aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259918} {:answer/id #uuid "220b8b83-724a-5cbe-853b-6caa42638775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260170} {:answer/id #uuid "726ac3fa-740a-5e90-81fa-f599fc3f37a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260875} {:answer/id #uuid "81ca9339-6bce-5219-8fae-787545463a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6b36bf-bffd-5918-ae53-d958ad6e391a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261101}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45caafc-858f-500e-9ef9-058205b847f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cb6a7e0a-d356-5b58-a703-e0864f9a1a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-128500" :question/problem "Given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{vmatrix}-5\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183c086d-012b-5f39-b92e-4550955dfcbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260085} {:answer/id #uuid "2044861f-98f6-51d9-9cf5-e5080be450a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260152} {:answer/id #uuid "21a46985-36f6-5f1d-b213-16f3935ec5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260165} {:answer/id #uuid "91c5f6e6-19cd-5455-92f6-06f29a9d6687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261142} {:answer/id #uuid "c0800f44-af37-5d5d-b586-92ebc2148392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a39ba2f-181c-558b-b3c6-6fdf22cdca96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9517ddd6-18dd-5bea-948b-a75416c96cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-128502" :question/problem "Given that \n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nand $det(C)=28,$ find the value of $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}q & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (q+25)-3\\cdot (-1)+5 \\\\  & =2q+58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $28,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q+58 & =28 \\\\ 2q & =-30 \\\\ q & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d545a5-b2e6-5053-b8b6-37194c5c9aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263315} {:answer/id #uuid "338b8f0e-6e8c-5003-a20f-65d3696dd73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} {:answer/id #uuid "40cea55b-6167-57c5-a2d6-7f87677038d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263572} {:answer/id #uuid "53864c34-56a3-5553-afb8-033b263dcdea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263719} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bc1bd7-12d4-51d7-8d46-edc046b147b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264868}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f084fe2-5f6e-5af3-b0dc-03f636f5e40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78f7d23e-60ed-507c-b4f6-6101bce65778" :question/math-academy-id "q-129495" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=2\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,10=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30980b36-8778-5a51-89b8-a81fc027883f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263413} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd13396-77b3-54fa-8ae9-6c7200fc84bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263533} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0eeffe-95e5-570e-9c36-aea6b4fd89db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264086} {:answer/id #uuid "975b44bb-df10-5292-a437-e855bf7bd551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264299} {:answer/id #uuid "aee8c241-2555-5612-b6c3-afa60e199249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263413} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f5a069b-5bd2-5270-9936-a86902646679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "910b9da2-b0da-578c-b6de-5df3df9fdc3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129496" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Y,$ so $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={XY}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $XY,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,22=5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle XY=\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e376d53d-27f0-5be2-b35f-f4d91876ada1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264977} {:answer/id #uuid "eb678b62-e5ac-5a34-a142-98bf42189475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265054} {:answer/id #uuid "f85d4f26-7a1c-53cb-bb4f-7d6a715d2393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265174} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcf0048-3a05-5c6a-a8a8-728a7671810b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265204} {:answer/id #uuid "fd313f4f-a74a-5051-a216-9b54910390f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265223}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265054} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad6ed81-a246-516c-a457-e881158c431f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c109d94f-badb-560f-816a-dc72e0193e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129961" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthen $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=(-3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=(-3)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a9b3cc-7576-59b2-aabd-3e3baec2350f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263163} {:answer/id #uuid "220549d6-0043-5ea3-afc4-aec900485a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263301} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba621a6-7f8a-5196-8dc2-e27ffc2bb0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263369} {:answer/id #uuid "c860a24f-7231-5ddb-8c12-1297c7899912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264755} {:answer/id #uuid "e89a0dc1-39c3-5234-b0bd-01580a7b5954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265022} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b13e3a0-f57b-544f-a120-5165f77a15ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "945d4e42-e131-5958-8aed-5486accd9a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-130111" :question/problem "Let $S=UV.$ What is the value of ${s}_{13}$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The full matrix product is\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the $1$st row in $U$ by the $3$rd column in $V$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{13} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-6-6+5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41cfda0a-f144-589a-a43c-f062ef97cc0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263582} {:answer/id #uuid "6754aa3f-9d7e-5ec5-8d62-0bc2e16b1dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263893} {:answer/id #uuid "8692590c-83fe-5fc5-a3dc-acaa0e379556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264160} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7c5d22-55ac-5c2e-8365-30562490fd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264790} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ee5f0e-8ece-5209-a013-26fe841fffb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265142}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263582} :answer-field/id #uuid "913f5424-fdc7-501c-8672-ca7479ea1e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "131c2176-2405-5c54-b473-9fb3958cf472" :question/math-academy-id "q-130120" :question/problem "Let $D=AB.$ What is the value of ${d}_{24}$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The full matrix product is\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the $2$nd row in $A$ by the $4$th column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{24} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-9+4+3 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
